// made by build_talk.py from lines-A.json and lines-B.json: do not edit by hand
window.MF_LINES = {"people":{"old-lamp-seller":{"guess":"That wisps are flames that slipped their wicks and went looking for another, since a flame only ever borrows its wick.","invented":["She cuts and twists every wick she sells herself, and has trimmed wicks since she was six.","She cut four of the wicks in the captain's ship lamps.","She has sent the lamplighter wicks for the dead post for twenty years and keeps a tally; the one Io carries is the three hundredth.","Her mother told her the second half of a wick always burns quicker.","Tonight she keeps a chalk mark on her counter for every lamp the four bring home."],"lines":[{"id":"old-lamp-seller-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"Evening. I've held up a feather, shut my wagon door and stood in front of them. They still lean. Your turn, Jester.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"There you are at last. I've cut every wick on this counter short, so there's less flame for anything to get hold of.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"You've gone past my stall nine times tonight. On the tenth, I thought, she'll stop. And here you are.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"A flame leans for wind, or a door, or somebody breathing on it. I've never seen one lean for nothing. Not in my life.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Two of those cold lights came through at supper. Every flame on my counter shrank to a bead till they'd gone.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"The captain's lamps? I cut four of those wicks. A good wick never leaves its lamp. Something took them by the flame.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"My guess? Those cold lights are flames that slipped their wicks. A flame only ever borrows a wick, you know.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've sold nine lamps tonight. Nobody buys a lamp at night. They want something to hold, I think, not to light.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've a chalk mark on the counter for every lamp you bring home. Don't make me run out of counter.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Twelve home and tied down with blue thread. I'd have built wire cages. Twelve of them. I'd still be at it.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"My flames still lean, mind. Less. Like someone told to sit down who keeps looking at the door.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"Every flame in the square is lying near flat toward that hill. I've stopped trimming. You can't trim for that.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"I've counted every minute since the ship went up. I'll not tell you how many. Sit, before I start again.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Thirty-one flames on my counter, standing straight up. I've never been so glad of a dull flame in my life.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Somebody will have to keep that new flame on the crag. It'll want a decent wick. I've set my best aside.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Twice in one night. Don't cast near my counter, mind. When you do, every flame I've got bows down to the wick.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"I've put a wick by for your wagon lamp. Short, tight twist. It's the sort that stays where it's put.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"My hands have trimmed wicks since I was six and never once shook. Tonight they shook. Twice. I counted.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You've stood at my stall more tonight than the captain has in all his years, and he buys wicks.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"Won, have you? You've come back brighter than you went. I notice a flame grow by a hair, and I noticed.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lost"},"text":"Knocked flat, and upright again already. I'd sell a wick that did that for double.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"One of you is burning low. A quarter of a wick left, I'd say. Rest before you gutter.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"Your stool's been empty so long a cat took it. I've moved the cat.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"old-lamplighter"},"text":"You've been out to the lamplighter. Did she ask after me? No. She'll have asked after the wick.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"fortune-teller"},"text":"The fortune-teller's had you in, then. She'll have charged a coin to tell you it's dark out. I'll tell you for nothing.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wick"},"text":"The right size for once, she says? It's the same size I've sent her for twenty years. The cheek of the woman.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wisp-warmed"},"text":"So Io warmed one till it went home? Then they want a wick to come back to. I've a drawerful.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"New wicks, you four. Bright, and a bit too eager. That burns down to something steadier.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"I used to lose three flames every time you fought in the ring. Now it's one. You've stopped wasting sky.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"When you four walk past now my flames stand up straight, like they're being inspected. They never did that for anyone.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[6,6]},"text":"Six. Exactly half. My mother always said the second half of a wick burns quicker. I hope she was right.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[11,11]},"text":"Eleven. One short. I can't abide a box of twelve with a gap in it. Go and fetch the last.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"errand":{"wick":"open"}},"text":"Has Io still got my wick? Tell her keep it in its paper. Damp is the end of a good wick.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"errand":{"wick":"done"}},"text":"Thank Io for walking it out. That's the three hundredth wick I've sent to that post. I keep a tally.","emote":"thanks"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"Hold still. I'm trimming, and if I look up I'll cut it crooked. Talk to my hands."},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"watch"},"text":"Hush a moment. I'm counting how far they lean. I like to know a thing exactly before I'm frightened of it.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Lamps and wicks! Good tight wicks!"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"Your stool's still here, fool!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"Chalk's ready, Jester! Bring me another!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"old-lamp-seller-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Wicks! Even fools need wicks!","emote":"point"}]},"ribbon-dyer":{"guess":"That wisps are colour that never took: flame that was never fixed, so it runs at the first chance, what his trade calls fugitive.","invented":["His hands have been blue to the wrist since he was a boy.","He has kept the same blue vat going for forty years and feeds it every night.","He has never once got the colour of the sky after dark in a pot.","He dyed the blue cloth of the fortune-teller's tent.","He keeps a scrap of every colour he ever made in a box.","He held back one hand's length of the blue he sold the Fox."],"lines":[{"id":"ribbon-dyer-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"Evening. I bow because I'm old, and it's quicker than talking.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"You've been out on the moor. It's on your boots. Peat brown. Good honest colour, that.","emote":"point"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"Late to meet. Never mind. Some colours take all night to come up.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"The cold lights have no colour I could name. Not white. Not grey. Like water the dye's been washed out of.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"The flames in the square have all gone a shade thinner. Yellow going to straw. A dyer sees it.","emote":"point"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"I've a word for them, for what it's worth. Fugitive. In my trade that's a colour that never took. It runs.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"My steam doesn't lean now. It streams out toward the gate like a ribbon off a pole. And no wind to fly it.","emote":"point"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've stopped dyeing. Nothing takes tonight. Red went in the pot, came out pink, and paled on the line.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I kept back a hand's length of the Fox's blue. Habit. It's the only thing in my stall that hasn't faded tonight.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Still leaning, the flames. But they've got their colour back. Gold, not straw.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Blue holds because it sat a month in the vat. Nothing about it was quick. Except the Fox.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"I can't watch the hill. I fold ribbon instead. I've folded this lot four times.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"I've put a lid on the pot. First time ever. I didn't want to see which way the steam went.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Steam's going straight up. I put my hand in it to be sure. Scalded myself. Worth it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"That light on the crag. Small, warm yellow. I'll try for it in the pot tomorrow. I'll get it wrong.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"You came back. People don't, to me. I say so little they think I'm cross.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"I've a scrap of every colour I ever made, in a box. I'll show you one day. Not tonight.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"I'll tell you. Forty years I've tried to dye the sky after dark. Never got it. You walk about in it.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You again. Stand by the pot long enough and you'll come out a different colour.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"You won. There's colour up in your face. Good. Keep it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lost"},"text":"Went under, did you. Cloth's the same. Goes in the pot dull, comes up better.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"Somebody's gone pale. I know pale. I've made forty shades of it, and that's the worst.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"Long enough gone for me to feed the vat twice. Welcome back.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"fortune-teller"},"text":"You've been to the star tent. That blue's mine. She tells people it's the night sky. It's a week in my vat.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"pie-seller"},"text":"The pie-seller. Flour on her, always. Flour's the one white that never comes out. I've tried.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"stitched"},"text":"Twelve stitches of my blue, they tell me, holding twelve flames. Best work it ever did.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wisp-warmed"},"text":"Held in her hands till it warmed, then off home. That's how you fix a colour, near enough. Heat and patience.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"Still wet from the pot, you four. Bright. It'll shift a bit before it sets.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"You four have set. Whatever comes tonight, it won't wash out of you now.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"Somebody asked me what you four are like. I said deep blue, all the way through. They didn't follow.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[6,11]},"text":"More lamps home than out. I've put a red in the pot to see if it'll take. It's taking. Slowly.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[12,12]},"text":"Twelve. I sold the Fox blue enough for twelve and a bit. I don't know how she knew. I didn't ask.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"thread"},"text":"Let me see that. It twitches toward the hill. And no colour in it at all. That's not thread, then.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"amulet"},"text":"Warm like my vat on a good morning. That's something that's been kept, not lit.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"I'm stirring. If I stop, it streaks. Speak. I'll listen."},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"watch"},"text":"Watch the steam with me a moment. No, don't talk. Just watch where it goes."},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Hot pot. Step wide."},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"Evening, night-blue.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Hold fast, out there.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ribbon-dyer-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"A nod. I'm stirring.","emote":"nod"}]},"fortune-teller":{"guess":"That somebody has laid a fire nobody came to, and the wisps are its invitations going out.","invented":["She keeps a tin for coins from true readings, and it sat empty for thirty years.","She owns only one fire card and has turned it for thirty years without believing it.","Her deck has a card numbered nothing that she thinks looks like the Jester.","The stars on her tent are painted on.","The captain has never once paid for a reading.","She keeps a cushion for people who have had bad news.","She sells charms, and hers are kept warm up her sleeve."],"lines":[{"id":"fortune-teller-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"Come in, come in. I'd like to tell you a pleasant lie, and tonight I can't find one anywhere.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"fortune-teller-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"So you're the fool who's fetching lamps. The cards told me. I'd like it noted that I didn't want them to.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"fortune-teller-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"At last. Every customer tonight has asked me about you four, and I've had to say I don't know. Humiliating.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"fortune-teller-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Eleven shuffles, and the fire card on top every time. I only own the one.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"fortune-teller-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"The stars on my tent are painted on. I want that understood. Tonight I keep looking up at them anyway.","emote":"point"},{"id":"fortune-teller-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Twelve lamps gone east. I'd have warned the captain for a coin. He has never once paid for a reading.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"fortune-teller-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Here's a reading, free. Somebody laid a fire and nobody came. Those lights are the invitations going out.","emote":"think"},{"id":"fortune-teller-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've stopped charging. Being right feels too much like stealing.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"fortune-teller-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I turned a card for the baker just now. A good one. I nearly kissed him. I nearly kissed the card.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fortune-teller-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"All twelve home, and the deck's gone quiet. I don't trust a quiet deck. It's thinking.","emote":"think"},{"id":"fortune-teller-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"The fire card came up last tonight, not first. I've done this a long time. I'm calling that progress.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fortune-teller-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"I won't deal while you're up there. Not one card. If it's bad, I don't want to be the one who knew.","emote":"refuse"},{"id":"fortune-teller-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"There's a card in my deck numbered nothing. It comes first and it comes last. It looks very like you.","emote":"point"},{"id":"fortune-teller-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"I turned the fire card again just now. Same paint, same fire. It looks less lonely. Paint doesn't do that.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"fortune-teller-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"I've no idea what to charge for tonight. That has never happened. I may give it all back.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"fortune-teller-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Back again. Second visits are half price. I've only just decided that. Tell nobody.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fortune-teller-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"Your sharp-eyed one is watching my hands. Tell her the cards are honest tonight. It's me that usually isn't.","emote":"think"},{"id":"fortune-teller-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"My secret. I keep a tin for coins from true readings. It sat empty for thirty years.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fortune-teller-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You're in here so often I ought to charge you rent. Sit. The chair's warm. It knows you.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"fortune-teller-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"You won. I could have told you that. I'm glad I didn't have to.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fortune-teller-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lost"},"text":"Flat on your back, I hear. I didn't see it coming, if that helps. I usually say I did.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"fortune-teller-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"One of you is hurt. Sit her down. I keep a cushion for people who've had bad news.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"fortune-teller-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"Where did you get to? I dealt for you while you were gone. You were fine. I checked twice.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fortune-teller-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"ballad-singer"},"text":"You've talked to the singer. She'll want a last verse out of you. Don't promise one you can't pay for.","emote":"point"},{"id":"fortune-teller-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"gate-keeper"},"text":"You've met the gate keeper. I read for the gate keeper once. Every card came up coins. Nobody was surprised.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fortune-teller-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"stitched"},"text":"Blue thread on the captain's lamps, I hear. I've no card for blue thread. I looked.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"fortune-teller-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wraith-down"},"text":"You put down the dark thing on the road? I'd have charged three coins to foretell that. I'd never have dared.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"fortune-teller-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"The hard cards are new to you four. No shame. Everyone's new once. I was new for years.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fortune-teller-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"People come in asking how far you four will go. I've had to raise my prices.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fortune-teller-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"I tried to read your fortunes just now. The cards ran out before you did.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"fortune-teller-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[1,1]},"text":"One home. In my trade one good card means nothing. Two is a pattern. Bring me two.","emote":"point"},{"id":"fortune-teller-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[12,12]},"text":"All twelve. I'd have said eleven, to be safe. I'm in the business of being safe. You clearly aren't.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fortune-teller-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"glass"},"text":"Cold glass. Hold it to your eye and tell me what you see. No, don't. I've had enough truth for one night.","emote":"refuse"},{"id":"fortune-teller-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"amulet"},"text":"That's not one of mine. Mine are warm because I keep them up my sleeve. That one's warm on its own.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"fortune-teller-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"One moment, I'm shuffling. It calms my hands. Not tonight, but usually."},{"id":"fortune-teller-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"chat"},"text":"Do forgive me. I was telling someone their future, and it was going badly for both of us.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"fortune-teller-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Futures told! Tonight, sadly, true!","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"fortune-teller-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"No charge for you, fool!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"fortune-teller-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Don't make me right, Jester!","emote":"point"},{"id":"fortune-teller-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Palms read! Prices high!"}]},"ballad-singer":{"guess":"That lights follow a tune out over the moor, the way they do in the old songs, and she half fears her crag song started them.","invented":["She learned the crag song from her grandmother, who never knew who made it.","The crag song has a verse about an iron charm on a bracket.","She practises her bow in front of the four's wagon when they are out.","She tells each of the four, privately, that they are her favourite."],"lines":[{"id":"ballad-singer-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"Oh. It's you. Sorry, I go silly round you four. You're the act everyone stays for.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ballad-singer-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"You're the ones out on the moor tonight. Everyone's talking. I've already started a verse. Sorry.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"I've been working up the nerve to talk to you all night. Now it's late and I've forgotten every word.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ballad-singer-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"I sang the crag song at dusk, and right after, the candles started leaning. I'm not singing it again.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"ballad-singer-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"The crowd keeps looking east between verses. Every singer knows that look. It means they're somewhere else.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"ballad-singer-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"In the old songs, lights always follow a tune out over the moor. I've stopped singing anything slow. Just in case.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ballad-singer-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Twelve lamps went off together, they say. Like a chorus coming in on one breath. Horrible. Beautiful. Both.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"ballad-singer-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've switched to marching songs. Loud ones. People can't be frightened and clap at the same time.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"If I stop singing, the square goes so quiet you can hear the candles straining east.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"ballad-singer-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Twelve home. In a song this is where they cheer and the sad part starts. Please don't let it be that sort of song.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"ballad-singer-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"I've started a last verse for the crag song. One line. I've crossed it out four times. It keeps ending too soon.","emote":"think"},{"id":"ballad-singer-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"Nobody's watching me sing. They're all watching the hill. It's the first time I haven't minded.","emote":"point"},{"id":"ballad-singer-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"You're meant to be on after me. I've sung everything I know twice. I'm keeping your spot warm.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ballad-singer-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"The candles stood up straight in the middle of my chorus and I forgot every word. I didn't care.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"The crag song can have a last verse now. I've not written it. I want to hear how it really went first. From you.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"ballad-singer-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Again? Oh good. Don't tell the others, but you're my favourite of the four. I tell all of you that.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"You laugh in the wrong places. That's where the best lines are, you know. Nobody else ever hears them.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"Can I tell you something? I practise my bow in front of your wagon when you're out. Is that strange?","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ballad-singer-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You'll end up in a song if you keep coming round. I'll make you rhyme with something silly.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"You won? Already? I'd barely got the first verse of it written.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"ballad-singer-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lost"},"text":"Knocked flat? Good. Every proper ballad has that bit. It's the bit just before the good bit.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ballad-singer-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"Who's hurt? Come here. I'll sing you something soft. I promise nobody dies in it.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"ballad-singer-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lamp"},"text":"A lamp's come home since I saw you? That's another verse, then. This song's getting longer than the crag song.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"fortune-teller"},"text":"Did she turn you a card? She told me once I'd be famous. I think she says it to every singer and means none of us.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"chestnut-roaster"},"text":"The roaster told you his story? Count how often it changes. I've got three versions in my head already.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"pie"},"text":"The captain got his pie? Good. Every song needs one person in it who gets fed and goes home happy.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"first-lamp"},"text":"One lamp home, they're shouting. I lost my place in the verse and nobody minded. That's never happened.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"ballad-singer-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"You four are still in the first verse. It's my favourite verse. Everything can still happen.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ballad-singer-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"The ring crowd has started singing about you four. Badly. I'll fix the words later.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"There'll be songs about you four when I'm an old woman. I'd like at least one of them to be mine.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"ballad-singer-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[3,3]},"text":"Three home. Three's a good number. It's where people listening start to believe it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"ballad-singer-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[12,12],"stage":[3,4]},"text":"All twelve. I'll put them in one by one. It'll be long. I know I said I'd keep it short.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"charm"},"text":"An iron charm from the tower? The crag song has a verse about one. I always thought we'd made that up.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"ballad-singer-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"stone"},"text":"That's from the rush lad's fire? Somebody should write him a song. I will. He'll hate it.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"Sorry, I was mid-verse. I'll finish it later. It doesn't end well anyway."},{"id":"ballad-singer-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"rest"},"text":"I'm resting my voice. Which means I'll talk to you for ages. It's a known problem.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"ballad-singer-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Gather round! One more verse!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"ballad-singer-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"There's my favourite fool!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"ballad-singer-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Come home safe! I've no ending yet!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"ballad-singer-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Clap along, Jester!","emote":"laugh"}]},"fair-baker":{"guess":"Heat that went up somebody's flue and never found the way back down; once he hears a wisp was warmed and went home, lost heat looking for its own oven.","invented":["His grandmother built his oven, and in sixty years it never tried to leave before tonight.","He bakes the fair's bread for the road through the night.","Once the Jester has been by a few times he keeps a bun on the corner of the cart for her, and he hides his good knife.","He marks each lamp that comes home in the flour on his board."],"lines":[{"id":"fair-baker-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"Evening, bells. Have a bun before the oven pulls it up the flue. I'm only half joking.","emote":"wave"},{"id":"fair-baker-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"You look half frozen, bells. Stand by the oven a minute. Whatever she's pulling at, she's still got warmth for four.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"fair-baker-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"Bells, at last. Years you've walked past my cart, and it took a night like this to stop you. Bun. Still warm.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Every bun in this tray has risen lopsided, all leaning east. I've baked forty thousand buns and never a lopsided one.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"fair-baker-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"I've shut the damper right down and she still draws. Like she's heard somebody calling her name.","emote":"think"},{"id":"fair-baker-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Want to know what I reckon? Heat that went up somebody's flue and never found the way back down. That's them.","emote":"think"},{"id":"fair-baker-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"She pulls so hard the door rattles on its latch. I've wedged it with the rolling pin. She's not having my door.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've stood here since you went out, peel in one hand and poker in the other. My arms have gone to dough.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"fair-baker-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"My grandmother built this oven. In sixty years the old girl never tried to leave. She's trying tonight. I won't have it.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"fair-baker-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"She's still drawing, but soft now. Like a sigh, not a shout. Something out there has let go a little.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fair-baker-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"I've hung the peel back on its hook. First time since dusk. I'm keeping one eye on it, mind.","emote":"point"},{"id":"fair-baker-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"I've damped her down to embers so there's less for it to take. Worst bread I've made in years. Worth it.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"fair-baker-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"Take a bun back up with you. If anything up there gets close, throw it hard. It's yesterday's.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"She draws like an oven again. Only an oven. I'll have the road's bread done by morning after all.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fair-baker-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"First tray all night that rose straight up. You did that, bells. Don't ask me how I know. A baker knows.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Back already? Then the bun was good. I knew it was. I just like to hear it.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"I've started keeping a bun on the corner for you. Don't tell your three. They'll all want a corner.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fair-baker-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"You know which jar's the honey and where I hide the good knife. That makes you family at this cart.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"fair-baker-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"Once more and I'm putting you to work. Apron's on the hook. Mind the peel, it has opinions.","emote":"point"},{"id":"fair-baker-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"You've the look of someone who's won. Have the one with the most currants. That's the winner's bun.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"One of you is walking stiff. I've nothing for that but bread and sympathy, and you can have both.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"fair-baker-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"Where've you been, bells? I've had a bun going cold for you since two trays ago.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"fair-baker-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lamp"},"text":"Brought another one home? I'll mark it in the flour with the others. There. That's yours, the crooked one.","emote":"point"},{"id":"fair-baker-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"old-night-watchman"},"text":"In all the years I've known the watchman he never took a bun off me. Tonight he took two. That's how I know it's bad.","emote":"think"},{"id":"fair-baker-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"farm-lad"},"text":"You've been out to the farm lad? Tell him there's a loaf here with his name on it. Well. With my thumb in it.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wisp-warmed"},"text":"Your herb-witch held one till it warmed, and it went home? Lost heat, like I said. Heat always wants its own oven.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fair-baker-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"card"},"text":"The fortune-teller turned you the card with the empty fire? Not round here. There's always somebody stood by my fire.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"fair-baker-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"You four look like you came out of the oven early. Soft in the middle. No offence meant, bells.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"You've got a crust on you now, the four of you. You walk past my cart like you know where you're going.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fair-baker-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"When I'm old I'll tell folk I fed you. They won't believe me. I'll show them the peel. It proves nothing.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[1,5]},"text":"She was pulling like a horse at dusk. Now it's more like a goat. Bring a few more and she'll be a cat.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[12,12]},"text":"Twelve home. I baked twelve rolls, one for every lamp. That's a lie. I baked twelve and ate three.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"fair-baker-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"stone"},"text":"That stone's warmer than my oven floor tonight. Lend it me an hour and I'll bake you a loaf on it.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"fair-baker-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"amulet"},"text":"Warm like dough when it's proving. That's the best warm there is. Keep it close, bells.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"fair-baker-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"Can't stop, she's on the turn. Talk while I knock these back. You can knead if you're bored.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"fair-baker-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"rest"},"text":"Sitting down for the first time since noon. The oven can pull on its own a minute. There's flour sack enough for two.","emote":"wave"},{"id":"fair-baker-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Buns! Hot buns! Mind your fingers!"},{"id":"fair-baker-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"Bells! Eat something, you're all jingle!"},{"id":"fair-baker-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Come near my oven and you'll get the peel!"},{"id":"fair-baker-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Fresh out! Come and smell that!"}]},"old-night-watchman":{"guess":"Stragglers: every fair has someone out after the lamps who can't find their own wagon, and the cold things look like that to him, lost and not wicked.","invented":["He has walked the rows for forty years, and before tonight he never once had to go back on a round.","He bought his first wick from the lamp-seller as a lad, and she counted his change twice.","He has a bad leg of his own.","Tonight he hung a second lamp on every ring post, and later wired the ring lamps to their posts."],"lines":[{"id":"old-night-watchman-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"You four, is it. The ring's yours when you want it. Losing costs nothing. You'll wake by your own wagon, none the worse.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"Out past the gate at this hour. I'd tell you not to, but you'd go anyway. Sit on the ring rope a minute.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"So you came back down. Good. I don't say good to many people. Ask anyone.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Forty years I've latched shutters. I know a loose one by the sound. Tonight they're all latched and all rattling east.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Trimmed every wick on this row before dusk. Trimmed them straight. Look at them now, leaning like I'd been drinking.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Started my round at the square. Got to the ring and the square was dark again. I've never had to go back before.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Every fair there's somebody out after the lamps who can't find their wagon. Those cold things look like that to me.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"They put it out, I light it. They put it out, I light it. I've more flint than they've got night.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've hung a second lamp on every ring post. If the cold ones want to stop somewhere, they'll stop where you can reach.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"The shutters have stopped rattling. The lamps still lean, but the shutters have stopped. I'll take the shutters.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"You've the look of folk about to go where they shouldn't at night. I've seen it plenty. Go anyway. Come back.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"Every shutter's shut. Every lamp's lit. That's all a watchman can do. The rest went up that hill with you.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"They're leaning worse than at dusk. I've wired the ring lamps to their posts. Don't laugh. It's mostly working.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Walked the whole round and not one went out behind me. Felt wrong. I kept looking back like a fool.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Lost, I always said. Now every one of them's found its way, and I didn't have to walk a single one home.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Back, is it. The ring's still there. So am I. Neither of us is going anywhere tonight.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"One rule in my ring. Get up after. Everything else is bruises and opinions.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"You know my round now. Shutters first. Then lamps. Then you, it turns out.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"Every round tonight I get to this post and there you are. I've started counting you as one of my lamps.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"Won, did you. I'll bet you stood in front of the other three the whole time. Daft. Don't change it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lost"},"text":"Woke by the wagon? That's the ring's one kindness. Cost you nothing but a sore head. Now go and do it properly.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"One of yours is favouring a leg. I know that walk, I've got it myself. Get her seen to before the next bout.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"Thought you'd gone off east with the lamps. I checked your wagon twice. Don't make a thing of it.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"old-lamp-seller"},"text":"The lamp-seller sold me my first wick when I was a lad. Counted my change twice. Still does, every time.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"pie-seller"},"text":"The pie-seller shouts at the dark like it owes her money. I've not seen it argue back yet.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wraith-down"},"text":"They say the thing on the road at the stones is gone. Good. I never trust anything that stands still on a road at night.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wick"},"text":"The lamplighter's new wick went out on the dead post, I hear. She'll light it again tomorrow. So would I.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"Your bouts last long enough for me to trim all four ring lamps. That'll change. Keep at it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"The cold ones used to stop at my ring for the warm. Now they see you four in it and think twice.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"Forty years I've told fighters in that ring to mind their feet. I've nothing to tell you four. I don't like it.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[2,8]},"text":"Since your lamps started coming home I only go back for every other post. That's a good night, for tonight.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[12,12]},"text":"Twelve, is it. Then the captain flies. I've never trusted a ship at night. I trust that man, mind.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"glass"},"text":"Lantern glass, and cold with it. Not one of mine. Mine are all on their posts, and I'd know.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"charm"},"text":"A keeper's charm. Hung so the flame would know they'd be back. I've never needed one. I just come back.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"walk"},"text":"Walk with me if you're talking. I'm three posts behind, and they won't wait.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"watch"},"text":"Watching the ring lamps. That one leans further than the rest. I want to know why before it goes.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Ring's open, you four. Step in any time."},{"id":"old-night-watchman-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"Evening, Jester. Still standing, then."},{"id":"old-night-watchman-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Light, you stubborn thing. Light!"},{"id":"old-night-watchman-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Mind the rope. It bites."}]},"pie-seller":{"guess":"They're hungry: cold, hungry things going where the warm is, with the same look as every lad who ever walked past her cart without his coin.","invented":["She has sold pies at the fair for twenty years.","She has grown sons, who were never round her cart as much as the Jester is tonight.","She keeps a slate for regulars who owe her.","Tonight, for once in her life, she gives pies away."],"lines":[{"id":"pie-seller-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"Look at you, all bones under all those bells. Here. Mutton. You can pay me when you're famous.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"pie-seller-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"You're the ones fetching the captain's lamps back. A pie each, and the bill goes to him.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"The state of you. Whatever you've been doing, you've been doing it hungry. Sit. Mutton.","emote":"point"},{"id":"pie-seller-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Sold eleven pies since dusk and every one went down quick. Folk eat fast when they're nervous. Good for trade.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"If you ask me, those cold things are hungry. I know a hungry face. I've been selling pies to it for twenty years.","emote":"think"},{"id":"pie-seller-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"A whole string of lights went over my cart, low. Tell me they weren't the captain's. Oh, love. They were, weren't they.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"pie-seller-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Nobody's buying. They're all down at the gate gawping east. You can't sell a pie to the back of a head.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"pie-seller-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I'm giving pies away to anyone who'll stand by my lamp. Company keeps it lit. Don't you dare tell anyone I'm giving.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"pie-seller-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"Something cold sat on my cart roof a whole minute. I banged a pan at it and it went. So did my lamp.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"pie-seller-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Folk are buying again. They come out when things settle, like snails after rain. I'll take a snail's coin.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"You're going somewhere tonight, the four of you. Then take a pie each, eat it on the way, and don't argue.","emote":"point"},{"id":"pie-seller-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"I've done my sums. Four of you, one captain, one hill and a lot of dark. I'm keeping five pies hot.","emote":"think"},{"id":"pie-seller-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"Still selling. If the sky falls in tonight, it'll fall on folk who've been fed and paid up.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"pie-seller-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Pies! Free pies! Don't look at me like that. Tonight I'm giving and tomorrow I'll be sorry.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"My lamp's sitting up straight like a child at table. I gave it a pie. It can't eat it. It's the thought.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"pie-seller-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Back for another? Thought so. Nobody stops at one of mine.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"You're getting a taste for it. That's how it starts. Next it's three a day and you're on my slate.","emote":"point"},{"id":"pie-seller-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"I've stopped charging you. Don't get used to it. I've stopped charging you tonight.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"pie-seller-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You're round here more than my own sons ever were. At least you eat what's put in front of you.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lost"},"text":"Knocked flat, were you? Nobody's knocked flat twice on a belly full of my mutton. Eat.","emote":"point"},{"id":"pie-seller-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"One of yours looks done in, and you're stood here talking to me. Hot food first. Heroics after. Go on.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"pie-seller-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"Where've you been? I saved you one, then I sold it. You were gone too long, love. Trade's trade.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"pie-seller-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lamp"},"text":"Another lamp on the captain's ship? Good. Now tell him to sit down. He'll wear a ditch round those posts.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"captain"},"text":"You've talked to the captain, then. Lamps this, lamps that. Did he say if he'd eaten? He never says.","emote":"think"},{"id":"pie-seller-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"fair-baker"},"text":"The baker calls his bread travelling bread. It travels because nobody eats it. Tell him I said so.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"stitched"},"text":"I hear your Fox sewed the captain's lights down with thread. I've sewn crusts shut for years. Nobody calls me a witch.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"lamps-gone"},"text":"Is it true all twelve of the captain's lamps went? Every one? That poor man. No wonder he's off his food.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"pie-seller-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"You walk like you're not sure the ground will hold you. More mutton. That's my answer to most things.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"pie-seller-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"You've filled out. Not in the waist, love. In the shoulders. In how you stand at my cart.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"pie-seller-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"Folk will boast they bought pies off the same cart as you. I'll be charging extra for that by next fair.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[1,5]},"text":"A few home. That's a few less for the captain to fret about. Fretting men don't eat, and I won't have that.","emote":"point"},{"id":"pie-seller-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[6,11]},"text":"More than half home. The captain'll be up that ladder humming. He hums when he's happy. Badly, mind.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"errand":{"pie":"open"}},"text":"That pie's for the captain, love, not for walking round the fair with. Mind it's still hot when it gets there.","emote":"point"},{"id":"pie-seller-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"errand":{"pie":"done"}},"text":"The captain ate it? Good. Did he say anything? No, don't tell me. Two words and red ears, I'll bet.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"Hot pies, love, hot pies. Talk quick, I've a queue of nobody behind you.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"pie-seller-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"chat"},"text":"Sorry, love, I was giving someone a piece of my mind. They'll want it back. Now, what can I do you for?","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"pie-seller-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Hot pies! Pay now, thank me after!"},{"id":"pie-seller-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"There's my girl! Eaten today?"},{"id":"pie-seller-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Shoo! Go and be cold somewhere else!"},{"id":"pie-seller-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Pies! Hot as they come!"}]},"gate-keeper":{"guess":"They have been sent for: folk do not all go one way through a gate unless someone has called them, and he would like to know who.","invented":["He writes everyone who passes the gate in a book, the four too, though they go free as the fair's own.","He and the watchman have nodded to each other every night for twenty years.","The coin tin on his table always comes out right.","There is a stool at the coin table that he has never once sat on.","He kept the gate bar down from dusk until the light showed on the crag."],"lines":[{"id":"gate-keeper-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"You. The troupe. You go in and out free. I write you down anyway.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"You're the four bringing the lamps back through my gate. I've a line in the book for each. Carry on.","emote":"point"},{"id":"gate-keeper-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"You. Out my gate and back more times tonight than anyone. That's not a complaint. It's a count.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Four cold lights out over the bar since dusk. I wrote them down. I don't know what to put under paid.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"gate-keeper-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"I look at faces coming in. Tonight every face keeps turning round to look east.","emote":"point"},{"id":"gate-keeper-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Folk don't all go one way unless they've been sent for. Those lamps were sent for. I'd like to know who by.","emote":"think"},{"id":"gate-keeper-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Out is free. I said that. I did not mean lamps.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"gate-keeper-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"Some cold lights come back in over the bar now. Going home, by the look. I count them. They don't pay either.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"gate-keeper-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've had the bar down since dusk. It stops nothing that flies. It's a matter of principle.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"gate-keeper-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"That blue thread on the captain's lamps. Had I owned some at dusk, nothing would have gone over my gate.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Fewer cold things on the road now. I'd still like a word with whatever's at the top of it.","emote":"point"},{"id":"gate-keeper-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"You came down by air, so you never passed my bar. I've counted you in anyway. Go and finish it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"Not a soul on the crag road. Bar down, eyes on it. That's my part. Yours is up there.","emote":"point"},{"id":"gate-keeper-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"There's a light on the crag. Not mine to count. I've counted it. One.","emote":"point"},{"id":"gate-keeper-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"I've put the bar up. First time since dusk. Don't read anything into it.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"gate-keeper-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Still you.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"You again. You've a column in the book now. It's narrow.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"You can stand on my side of the table. Don't touch the tin.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You've a page of your own in the book now. It's a long page. I've not minded writing it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"You won. I can tell. You came back the same number you went out.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"One of you is walking short. Sit her on my stool. I've never once sat on it. Somebody might as well.","emote":"point"},{"id":"gate-keeper-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"You were gone a while. I noticed. I notice everyone. That's all it is.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"gate-keeper-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lamp"},"text":"Another one in over the bar. That one I let through.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"farm-lad"},"text":"You've seen the farm lad, then. Went out by day for rushes and never came back in. His line's been open all day.","emote":"think"},{"id":"gate-keeper-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"old-night-watchman"},"text":"The watchman and I nod. Twenty years of nods. Tonight he stopped and said it was cold. I agreed. A long talk, for us.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"card"},"text":"The fortune-teller turned you the bad card, I hear. She took a coin for it. I'd have told you the same for nothing.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"gate-keeper-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"pie"},"text":"The captain got his pie, I hear. Walked past my table with gravy on his collar. I didn't mention it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"You four go out my gate like you're off picking mushrooms. I watch the road till you're back.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"Your faces don't change at the gate any more, going out or coming in. That's how I know.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"When you four go out, the road goes quiet for an hour. Nothing comes near my gate. I've written that down too.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[1,5]},"text":"Some ticked off. Your sharp-eyed one ticks them too, under her breath. We agree so far.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[12,12]},"text":"Twelve ticks. I underlined the total. I don't underline.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"thread"},"text":"That thread still pulls east. Cut, and it still wants to go. Some things you can't turn back at a gate.","emote":"think"},{"id":"gate-keeper-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"amulet"},"text":"Left on a stone, and nobody saw who. That would never happen at my gate.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"gate-keeper-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"watch"},"text":"Watching the road. Talk if you like. I won't look round.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"gate-keeper-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"Counting the tin. Wait. There. Right again. It's always right. What is it?","emote":"think"},{"id":"gate-keeper-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"In or out. Make your mind up."},{"id":"gate-keeper-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"You. Again. Go on, then."},{"id":"gate-keeper-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"You there! You haven't paid!"},{"id":"gate-keeper-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Mind the bar."}]},"chestnut-roaster":{"guess":"Fire that said yes: the lamps and the cold lights were asked and went, where his coals were asked and said no.","invented":["He keeps one coal from every place the fair has stood, in a tin.","Within the first hour after the lamps went he had told the story eleven times.","The fortune-teller will not read his cards any more, because he talked through the last reading.","He says the gate keeper laughed once, in spring, three fairs back."],"lines":[{"id":"chestnut-roaster-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"You four at my brazier. Sit. I'll tell you a thing about my coals, and you tell me a thing about you.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"Back off the moor? Come to the fire and tell me all of it. I'll tell it better tomorrow, but you tell it first.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"Here they are. I've been telling your story all night and you've never once heard it. Sit down, it's good.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Six people have told me their flame's leaning. I've started a list. Nobody's told me theirs is standing up straight.","emote":"think"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"The gate keeper's been staring east since dusk and won't say why. I've asked four times. That's three more than usual.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Here's what I think. My coals were asked and said no. Those cold lights are fire that said yes.","emote":"think"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"I've told the lamps going over eleven times now. Each time the lamps get bigger. By midnight they'll be cows.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"Every cold one that goes over, my coals go a bit grey and come back. Asked again. Still no. Good coals.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"Half the fair stands at my brazier now. Warmest spot by the gate, and I'm the best talker. In that order.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Twelve stitches of blue and one ring of the Fox's bell. I saw it. I've told it twice and I'm not tired yet.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"My coals haven't gone grey in an hour. I don't trust it. I keep poking them to check they're still mine.","emote":"think"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"They went grey again just now, and stayed grey longer. I blew on them like a madman. Be quick up there.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"Nobody to tell. Folk have gone quiet and gone to their wagons. A gossip with no one to tell is a man with chestnuts.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Red as a robin, my coals. I keep a coal from every place we stand, in a tin. Tonight's is the one that said no.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"I've told it to four people and they've told four each. By morning you'll have fought the moon and won.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Back for the end of the story? There isn't one. I keep adding bits.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"I've been keeping score of who's asked after you four. It's most of the fair. The rest are asleep.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"You know all my stories now. That's dangerous. You'll start telling them better than me.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You come by so often I've put you in the story. You're the bit where somebody comes by again.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"You won? Tell me how. Slowly. Leave nothing out. I'll put the good bits back in later.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lost"},"text":"Flat on your backs, the four of you? Don't tell the baker, he'll tell the whole row. Tell me. I'll tell it kindly.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"There you are. Three things happened while you were gone, and I had to tell them all to the gate keeper.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lamp"},"text":"Another lamp over the gate? I saw it come in. My coals jumped up to meet it like a dog at the door.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"fortune-teller"},"text":"The fortune-teller won't read for me any more. I talked through the last one. Every card. She had to sit down.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"gate-keeper"},"text":"The gate keeper laughed once. Three fairs back, in spring. I was there. I'm the only one who believes me.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wick"},"text":"I hear the lamplighter's new wick lit and went out. My coals came back. Hers didn't. Poor old post.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"beacon"},"text":"They say there's a light on the crag. I know. I was first to say so. Ask anyone. Don't ask the gate keeper.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"You've the look of folk with your first story still in you. Give it here. I'll mind it for you.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"Folk talk about you at my brazier now without me starting it. That's how I know you're somebody.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"They'll tell your story long after mine are forgotten. I don't even mind. Much. A bit.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[1,5]},"text":"Every lamp that comes over, I tell whoever's nearest. I told one to a pony. It took it very well.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[6,11]},"text":"Past half now. I've stopped telling folk it's hopeless. I never said hopeless. I said tricky.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"thread"},"text":"That thread twitches toward the crag. My coals did the same, just before they said no. Hold it tight.","emote":"think"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"stone"},"text":"Warm, that stone. Hold it by my coals a minute. Let them see what staying put looks like.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"Hold on, turning. Too late and they split. Too early and they sulk. Right. Go on.","emote":"think"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"chat"},"text":"Sorry, I was telling the gate keeper a story. Not listening. Never is. Now then, you.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Chestnuts! Free, and worth every bit!"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"Jester! Come and hear the new bit!"},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Stay red, you lot. Stay red."},{"id":"chestnut-roaster-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Hot chestnuts! Hot news!"}]},"captain":{"guess":"Deserters, lights that jumped ship; once he hears a beaten one was warmed and went home, crew lost overboard instead, to be hauled in, not hanged.","invented":["He reads the weather by his pennant.","When a lamp comes home he stands by its post a minute, and he has put a hand to every post.","He eats standing up."],"lines":[{"id":"captain-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"Evening. Mind the mooring lines, they're taut tonight. No wind to pull them. I've checked.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"You're the ones bringing my crew home. Thank you. I don't say it twice, so that'll have to last.","emote":"thanks"},{"id":"captain-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"We've not talked, you and me. You brought my lamps home. That's introduction enough.","emote":"greet_bow"},{"id":"captain-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"My lamps are leaning on their hooks. All twelve, the same way. Not a breath of wind, and the pennant hangs dead.","emote":"point"},{"id":"captain-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Clear sky, and the air's going east all the same. Slow, like a tide going out. I don't trust a tide in a field.","emote":"think"},{"id":"captain-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Twelve empty hooks. I keep counting them. They keep coming out twelve.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"captain-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Lost crew at ports before. Never all at once. Those cold lights going east? Deserters, I'd say. Jumped ship.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"captain-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"Each one home goes up on its post, and I stand by it a minute. Daft. A captain counts his crew back aboard.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"Rigging hums every time a cold one goes over. No wind in it. I know most weather. I don't know this.","emote":"think"},{"id":"captain-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Twelve on deck. Stitched down with blue. I've walked the rail twice and put a hand to every post.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Wind's fair, sky's clear, crew's all aboard. That's three things I couldn't say an hour ago.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4],"where":"W8"},"text":"Colder up here than the field. My lamps are burning small, like crew keeping their heads down. Good crew.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4],"where":"W8"},"text":"Tower's black as pitch. Wherever I stand her off, all twelve stay lit. You'll have something to aim at coming down.","emote":"point"},{"id":"captain-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Saw my lamps brighten when the crag lit. All twelve at once. Like crew answering a hail.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"captain-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Calm at last. When the fair moves on I'll take her out lit end to end, and dip to that light as I pass.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"You again. Good. I like a face that comes back.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"You come by regular as a harbour bell. I could set a glass by you.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"I'd let you take the helm, if I let anybody take the helm. I don't. But I'd think about it.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"captain-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You're aboard so often I'll have to sign you on. Pay's poor. Food's mutton.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"captain-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"Won, by the look of you. Good. Don't celebrate near my lamps. They've had enough excitement for one night.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"captain-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"One of yours is listing. Bring her aboard and sit her on a coil of rope. Best seat I've got.","emote":"point"},{"id":"captain-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away","where":"W3"},"text":"Long time gone. I watched the gate. Then the sky. Then the gate again.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lamp"},"text":"Another one home. One less I'm lying awake for. Go on. Fetch its mates.","emote":"thanks"},{"id":"captain-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"pie-seller"},"text":"The pie-seller's been at you about me, I suppose. Thinks I don't eat. I eat. Standing up.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"captain-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"gate-keeper"},"text":"The gate keeper and I agree on one thing. You count what you're trusted with. Every night, twice.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wisp-warmed"},"text":"Your herb-witch warmed one till it went home, I hear. Then maybe they're not deserters. Overboard, more like.","emote":"think"},{"id":"captain-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wraith-down"},"text":"Something stood on the road by the stones, and it's gone now? Good. A road's a channel. You keep it clear.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"You go out like a new crew. Loud, and all at once. You'll learn to go quiet.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"You're coming back steadier. Less noise, more done. That's a crew.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"I've flown through storms that frightened me less than you four. I mean that kindly.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"captain-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[1,5]},"text":"Bow's lit. Stern's dark. She looks like she's winking at me.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"captain-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[6,11]},"text":"More lit than dark now. I could fly her on that. I won't. Twelve or nothing.","emote":"shake_head"},{"id":"captain-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"errand":{"pie":"open"}},"text":"That's the pie-seller's mutton. I'd know it in a fog. Thank her, and tell her I'm eating it, so she can stop looking.","emote":"thanks"},{"id":"captain-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"errand":{"pie":"done"}},"text":"That pie's still sitting warm in me. If the pie-seller asks, tell her I sat down to eat it. It'll please her.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"captain-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"walk","where":"W3"},"text":"Walk with me. Post to post. It helps me think, and I've a lot to think about.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"captain-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"watch","stage":[2,4]},"text":"Watching my lamps. A good flame burns like it's listening to you. Tonight they're listening to something else.","emote":"point"},{"id":"captain-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Stand clear of the ladder, there!"},{"id":"captain-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"Ahoy, you four!"},{"id":"captain-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Hold, you lot. Hold fast."},{"id":"captain-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Keep your bells clear of my rigging!"}]},"old-lamplighter":{"guess":"That a wisp is a flame that was blown out careless instead of capped, so it never knew it was finished and went wandering.","invented":["Her mother taught her never to blow a lamp out, only to cap it.","Her round is forty-one lamps, from the fair gate out to the Last Lantern.","She saw the farm lad go up her track at noon, whistling, and has not seen him come back.","The lamp-seller once counted her wrinkles out loud.","She gives the dead post a minute after she lights it, every night, in case."],"lines":[{"id":"old-lamplighter-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"You've come out a long way, Jester. Most folk stop at the gate. My lamps don't, so I don't.","emote":"wave"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"You'll be the four, then. My round's forty-one lamps and I've not had a visitor at one of them in years.","emote":"wave"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"Took you till now to come and say hello. I don't mind. Lamps and old women, we're used to waiting.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"My lamp's leaning east and there's not a breath of wind. I've put my hand round it. It doesn't help. It's company.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Lit the dead post at dusk like always. Tonight I watched the flame leave. It didn't go out. It went.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"Those lights out in the heather want fetching. They're none of mine, but I'd not leave a dog out on a night like this.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"My mother said never blow a lamp out. Cap it. A blown flame doesn't know it's done. It wanders.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I'm not going back to the fair. Somebody has to stand here so the lights going home know where the road is.","emote":"refuse"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I watched your herb-witch hold one like a hurt bird till it went warm. All my years of lamps, I never thought to try.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"Heather's dark again. No lights in it but mine. That's how a moor ought to look at night.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"My lamp still leans, mind. I've tied my hanky round the post. Don't laugh. It's like holding its hand.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"I can see the ship up by the crag. Twelve lamps in a row, like a round. Somebody keep them lit.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"My lamp's tugging on its hook like a child that wants to go and look. I've told it no. It's sulking.","emote":"refuse"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"Both posts are lit. The dead one too. A light came down off the hill and sat in it like it had never been gone.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"That post's held since the light came down. I'm not crying, it's the smoke. There isn't any smoke.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"Come out twice, have you? Bring that cold over by the lamp. It'll see to you.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"My lamp likes you, I think. It burns a bit taller when you're stood there. Don't let it go to your head.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"You want to know why I light that dead post every night? Somebody has to. A lamp should know it's expected.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"Out here again. I've started leaving you the lee side of the post. The lamp's not pleased. That's its side.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"You won, by the look of you. Good. Now do your shouting further up the track. My lamp's nervous.","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"One of you's limping. Lean on my post a minute, love. It's held me up for years.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"Thought you'd gone. I kept the lamp up bright in case you needed finding.","emote":"wave"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lamp"},"text":"Another lamp got home, has it? Good. I don't like any lamp out on the moor with nobody to light it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"old-lamp-seller"},"text":"You've seen the lamp-seller. Is she still counting everything? She counted my wrinkles once. Out loud.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"farm-lad"},"text":"You found the rush lad by the pool? Is he warm? He went up my track at noon, whistling. I've not heard him since.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"lamps-gone"},"text":"Ship's lamps, the lights in my heather? No wonder they've no posts. Poor things, a long way off their hooks.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wraith-down"},"text":"That dark thing by the stones is gone? I felt it up there all evening. It never turned to my lamp. Only up the hill.","emote":"think"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"You four jump at every shadow on the track. Good. I did, my first year. It means you're looking.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"You walk this track like you've a round of your own now. Straight down the middle. No looking back.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"The heather goes quiet when you four come down the track. I've only ever heard it do that for weather.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[1,5]},"text":"Some home already? Good. I never sleep while there's a lamp out on this moor. Not that I sleep at night anyway.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[12,12]},"text":"All twelve. Not one of them stopped by my post to say goodnight. Ship's lamps. No manners.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"errand":{"wick":"open"}},"text":"Is that her wick your herb-witch is carrying? Bring it here, then. We'll watch it not work together.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"errand":{"wick":"done"}},"text":"Tell her the wick was good. I'll want another tomorrow. Don't tell her I said it was good.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"Hush a minute, I'm lighting. A flame likes quiet while it's catching."},{"id":"old-lamplighter-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"watch","stage":[0,4]},"text":"I'm watching the dead post. I always give it a minute after. In case. Stand with me.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Mind the ruts, there!","emote":"point"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"Evening, love! Lamp's still lit!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Go on. I'll keep the road lit!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"old-lamplighter-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{},"text":"Don't fight near my lamp!","emote":"cross"}]},"farm-lad":{"guess":"That wisps are lights nobody was watching: look away for one minute and off they go, which is why he will not take his eyes off his fire.","invented":["He has cut rushes for the fair's ponies since he was small, and they expect him home.","His lantern was his grandad's, and his grandad is still alive to hear about tonight.","It took him nine strikes of his flint to light the fire.","He went up the track at noon, whistling, past the lamplighter."],"lines":[{"id":"farm-lad-01","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[0,1]},"text":"Oh, it's you lot. It is, isn't it? From the fair? Sorry, I can't look up. I'm minding the fire.","emote":"wave"},{"id":"farm-lad-02","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[2,3]},"text":"The Jester. At my fire. Wait till the ponies hear. They won't care. I'll tell them anyway.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"farm-lad-03","slot":"hello","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[0,0],"stage":[4,5]},"text":"You've come all the way out here? To me? Nobody at the fair's going to believe it. I don't believe it. Sit down.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"farm-lad-04","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"My lantern went off up the hill like a pony that's heard the feed bucket. I never called it. Honest.","emote":"point"},{"id":"farm-lad-05","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[0,0]},"text":"Took nine goes with the flint to light this. Nine. It's not going anywhere now. I won't let it.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"farm-lad-06","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"If you ask me, they're lights nobody was watching. I looked away from my lantern for one minute. One.","emote":"think"},{"id":"farm-lad-07","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[1,1]},"text":"A string of lights came down over the far bank, like starlings settling. They've not moved since. I'm not going over.","emote":"point"},{"id":"farm-lad-08","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"I've had this fire going since the sun went. Is it still the same night? It feels like about four nights.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"farm-lad-09","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[2,2]},"text":"Saw a little light go back past me toward the fair, all warm and gold. I nearly waved at it. I did wave.","emote":"wave"},{"id":"farm-lad-10","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"The far bank's gone dark. No more lights in the reeds. Does that mean you've got them all? It does, doesn't it.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"farm-lad-11","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[3,3]},"text":"It's gone quieter. I heard a bird just now, first one all night. I nearly cried. I didn't. Nearly, though.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-12","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"I saw a ship go over toward the crag with all its lamps lit. Was that you? It was, wasn't it. I knew it.","emote":"point"},{"id":"farm-lad-13","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[4,4]},"text":"My fire's leaning up the hill harder than all night. I've got my boot against the stones. Feels like helping.","emote":"cross"},{"id":"farm-lad-14","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"I looked away just now. On purpose. Counted to ten. When I looked back it was still there. It just stayed.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-15","slot":"stage","kind":"talk","when":{"stage":[5,5]},"text":"There's a little light in the heather by my boot. I think it's my lantern's, come home. It's the right yellow.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"farm-lad-16","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[1,1]},"text":"You're back. I saved you the dry end of the log.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"farm-lad-17","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[2,4]},"text":"I've told the fire all about you. It went up a bit when I said the Jester. I'm not making that up.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-18","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[5,9]},"text":"Can I ask you something? Do you get frightened when you fight? You never look it. How do you not look it?","emote":"think"},{"id":"farm-lad-19","slot":"count","kind":"talk","when":{"talks":[10,99]},"text":"You come out here more than I go home. Have you got a fire of your own you're avoiding?","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-20","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"won"},"text":"Was that you? Did you win? You won. You've got the look the ponies get after a good gallop.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-21","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"lost"},"text":"You got knocked down? You? I didn't know you could fall over. I thought you sort of floated.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"farm-lad-22","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"hurt"},"text":"Sit down by the fire, all of you. It's a good fire. It's warm and it doesn't wander off.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"farm-lad-23","slot":"just","kind":"talk","when":{"just":"away"},"text":"You were gone that long I ran out of sticks and started on the rushes. The ponies will be furious.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"farm-lad-24","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"old-lamplighter"},"text":"The lamplighter's all right? Her lamp's still lit? I kept thinking of her down there on her own. She'd say she's fine.","emote":"think"},{"id":"farm-lad-25","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"met":"fair-baker"},"text":"You've been talking to the baker? Don't tell me what was in his oven. I'll only cry.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-26","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wraith-down"},"text":"It's gone off the road? Really gone? Then I could walk home. I'm not going to. But I could.","emote":"surprised"},{"id":"farm-lad-27","slot":"gossip","kind":"talk","when":{"heard":"wisp-warmed"},"text":"Your herb-witch warmed one and it went home? So they're not bad, they're lost. Like my lantern. Oh.","emote":"sad"},{"id":"farm-lad-28","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[1,4]},"text":"You four look a bit how I feel. No offence. I mean it nicely. Like you're still finding out.","emote":"shrug"},{"id":"farm-lad-29","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[5,14]},"text":"You walk like you know where your feet go. I tried walking like that. I fell in the rushes.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-30","slot":"level","kind":"talk","when":{"level":[15,20]},"text":"My grandad will want to hear about you. Every bit. I'll be telling it till I'm his age.","emote":"nod"},{"id":"farm-lad-31","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[7,11]},"text":"That's most of them back? Can I help carry? I'm good at carrying. I'd have to bring the fire.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-32","slot":"lamps","kind":"talk","when":{"lamps":[12,12]},"text":"All twelve? I want to shout. Can I shout? I'm going to shout. Quietly. The pool's listening.","emote":"laugh"},{"id":"farm-lad-33","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"stone"},"text":"That's my stone. Out of my fire ring. Is it still warm? It is. I'm going to be proud of that for years.","emote":"thanks"},{"id":"farm-lad-34","slot":"thing","kind":"talk","when":{"has":"thread"},"text":"That thread keeps twitching up the hill. Put it away, please. I don't want my fire getting ideas.","emote":"refuse"},{"id":"farm-lad-35","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"warm"},"text":"Come and warm up. There's room on the log. Only don't stand in front of the fire. I have to see it.","emote":"beckon"},{"id":"farm-lad-36","slot":"doing","kind":"talk","when":{"doing":"work"},"text":"One stick at a time. Too many and it roars, and roaring's how they start leaving. There. What is it?"},{"id":"farm-lad-37","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[0,0]},"text":"Hello! You're from the fair!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"farm-lad-38","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"talks":[3,99]},"text":"Jester! I kept it going!","emote":"wave"},{"id":"farm-lad-39","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[2,4]},"text":"Careful on that road, Jester!","emote":"point"},{"id":"farm-lad-40","slot":"bark","kind":"bark","when":{"stage":[0,4]},"text":"Still watching it!","emote":"point"}]}},"pairs":[{"id":"A-pair-01","who":["old-lamp-seller","ribbon-dyer"],"when":{"stage":[0,1]},"lines":[{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"Your steam's leaning the same way as my flames. I measured. Same angle, near enough."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"Near enough."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"You might say more than two words tonight, of all nights."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"I might. Then I'd have said them."}]},{"id":"A-pair-02","who":["fortune-teller","old-lamp-seller"],"when":{"stage":[0,1]},"news":"card","lines":[{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"I turned the fire card for the Jester. The one with nobody by it. She paid, and laughed."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"A fire with nobody by it. I've thirty-one of those on my counter. We call them lamps."},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"It isn't funny."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"No. Sit down. You're too tall to be frightened standing up."}]},{"id":"A-pair-03","who":["ballad-singer","fortune-teller"],"when":{"stage":[0,2]},"lines":[{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"Read me something nice. Anything. Make it up if you have to."},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"I don't make things up, darling. I arrange them attractively."},{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"Then arrange me something with a happy ending."},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"On a night like this? That's extra."}]},{"id":"A-pair-04","who":["ribbon-dyer","ballad-singer"],"when":{"stage":[0,1]},"lines":[{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"Have you any blue left? I wanted a bit for my hem before the four go on."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"The Fox has it."},{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"All of it? What on earth does she want with all of it?"},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"Sewing."}]},{"id":"A-pair-05","who":["old-lamp-seller","ballad-singer"],"when":{"stage":[1,2]},"lines":[{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"If I sing the crag song now, will your flames lean worse?"},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"Sing it and I'll count them."},{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"And if they do lean worse?"},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"Then sing something about sheep."}]},{"id":"A-pair-06","who":["fortune-teller","ribbon-dyer"],"when":{"stage":[1,3]},"lines":[{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"You dyed my tent. Be honest with me. Are the stars too much?"},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"Last year they were."},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"And tonight?"},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"Tonight I'd paint on more."}]},{"id":"A-pair-07","who":["old-lamp-seller","ribbon-dyer"],"when":{"stage":[1,3]},"news":"wick","lines":[{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"She lit my wick on the dead post. It leaned and went out. She says it's never the wick."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"It isn't."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"You've never even seen that post."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"I've seen your wicks."}]},{"id":"A-pair-08","who":["ballad-singer","ribbon-dyer"],"when":{"stage":[3,3]},"news":"stitched","lines":[{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"Did you hear? The Fox sewed every flame down with your blue. Twelve stitches."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"I heard."},{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"Aren't you proud? You should be shouting it from the awning."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"I am."}]},{"id":"A-pair-09","who":["fortune-teller","ballad-singer"],"when":{"stage":[4,4]},"lines":[{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"Deal one card for them. Just one. I won't hold you to it."},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"I dealt one when the ship went up. I put it back face down."},{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"You didn't look?"},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"Darling, I've been right all night. I'd like to be surprised once."}]},{"id":"A-pair-10","who":["old-lamp-seller","fortune-teller"],"when":{"stage":[5,5]},"lines":[{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"I've given three coins back tonight. Three. I don't know what's come over me."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"It's going round. I've given away two lamps and a box of wicks."},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"You counted them, I suppose."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"Forty-four wicks. I'll not ask for them back. I'll think about it."}]},{"id":"A-pair-11","who":["old-lamp-seller","old-night-watchman"],"when":{"stage":[0,2]},"lines":[{"by":"old-night-watchman","text":"Lamps keep going out behind me. Every row. I've relit your wicks three times tonight."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"It's not my wicks."},{"by":"old-night-watchman","text":"I know it's not. Forty years, and I've never had one of yours quit."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"Then it's something new. I've never cared for new."}]},{"id":"A-pair-12","who":["ribbon-dyer","pie-seller"],"when":{"stage":[1,3]},"lines":[{"by":"pie-seller","text":"Pie, love. You've had nothing since dusk. Don't tell me you have, I've been watching."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"I'm stirring."},{"by":"pie-seller","text":"Stir with one hand, eat with the other. It's mutton, before you ask."},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"I wasn't going to."}]},{"id":"A-pair-13","who":["fortune-teller","gate-keeper"],"when":{"stage":[1,2]},"news":"lamps-gone","lines":[{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"The captain's lamps came off their hooks and went over my bar. All twelve. East."},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"I know. I've had a card saying something of the sort since dusk."},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"Next time, tell the gate."}]},{"id":"A-pair-14","who":["ballad-singer","chestnut-roaster"],"when":{"stage":[1,3]},"lines":[{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"My coals went grey as those lamps went over, then came back. Put that in a song."},{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"What rhymes with coals?"},{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"Holes. Bowls. Moles."},{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"I'm not singing about moles. Not tonight. Maybe tomorrow."}]},{"id":"B-pair-01","who":["old-night-watchman","fair-baker"],"when":{"stage":[0,1]},"lines":[{"by":"old-night-watchman","text":"Your oven's drawing like a chimney fire. I can hear it from the ring."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"She wants to go somewhere. I keep telling her she lives here."},{"by":"old-night-watchman","text":"My lamps want the same. I tell them too. They don't listen either."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"Have a bun. No? Suit yourself. You always say no."}]},{"id":"B-pair-02","who":["pie-seller","fair-baker"],"when":{"stage":[0,1]},"lines":[{"by":"pie-seller","text":"Your oven's eating all the warm on this row. My pies go cold just standing here."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"Then sell them faster. You've the voice for it."},{"by":"pie-seller","text":"I've the voice. What I haven't got is anyone stopping. They all walk past looking up."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"Looking up's free. Buns cost. That's the trouble with tonight."}]},{"id":"B-pair-03","who":["chestnut-roaster","fair-baker"],"when":{"stage":[1,2]},"news":"lamps-gone","lines":[{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"Twelve of the captain's lamps, straight over my hat. Off their hooks and away east."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"Twelve? So that's what went over the row. I took it for sparks off my flue."},{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"Sparks go out. These kept going. Over the gate and up the crag road, the lot."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"My oven's been pulling that way all night. Same way they went."}]},{"id":"B-pair-04","who":["pie-seller","captain"],"when":{"stage":[1,1]},"lines":[{"by":"pie-seller","text":"You've lost your lamps and you've lost your colour. One of those I can fix."},{"by":"captain","text":"Is it the mutton?"},{"by":"pie-seller","text":"It's always the mutton. Eat it before you go chasing anything."}]},{"id":"B-pair-05","who":["chestnut-roaster","gate-keeper"],"when":{"stage":[4,4]},"lines":[{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"You've been staring at that crag since they went up. What are you watching for?"},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"Counting."},{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"Counting what? There's nothing up there to count."},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"Not yet."}]},{"id":"B-pair-06","who":["gate-keeper","captain"],"when":{"stage":[2,2]},"lines":[{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"How many on deck now? I want to check the book."},{"by":"captain","text":"Count them yourself. You will anyway."},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"I have. I wanted to hear you get it right."},{"by":"captain","text":"Dry as ship's biscuit, you are. Same number, then."}]},{"id":"B-pair-07","who":["old-night-watchman","gate-keeper"],"when":{"stage":[2,4]},"news":"flat","lines":[{"by":"old-night-watchman","text":"The four got knocked flat in my ring. Woke by their wagon, none the worse."},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"They didn't come through my gate flat."},{"by":"old-night-watchman","text":"Didn't say they did. Said they got up."},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"Good."}]},{"id":"B-pair-08","who":["chestnut-roaster","pie-seller"],"when":{"stage":[2,2]},"news":"first-lamp","lines":[{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"First of the captain's lamps came back over the gate. The four carried it in."},{"by":"pie-seller","text":"Did he eat when he got it? Tell me he ate."},{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"He took it up the ladder like a newborn. I didn't see him eat."},{"by":"pie-seller","text":"Men. Lamps first, mouths after."}]},{"id":"B-pair-09","who":["old-night-watchman","captain"],"when":{"stage":[0,0]},"lines":[{"by":"old-night-watchman","text":"Your lamps keeping their flames, captain? Mine won't stay lit past the next post."},{"by":"captain","text":"Mine lean. All twelve. But they're on hooks. They're staying."},{"by":"old-night-watchman","text":"I said that about mine an hour ago."}]},{"id":"B-pair-10","who":["fair-baker","gate-keeper"],"when":{"stage":[5,5]},"lines":[{"by":"fair-baker","text":"Have you seen it? A light on the crag. Small, but it's there."},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"I saw it first."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"Have a bun on it. Go on. Nobody's looking."},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"One. And I'm paying for it."}]},{"id":"B-pair-11","who":["old-lamp-seller","gate-keeper"],"when":{"stage":[1,2]},"lines":[{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"Twenty-six cold lights over the square since dusk. What do you make it at the gate?"},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"Twenty-eight."},{"by":"old-lamp-seller","text":"Then two came round the back of the tents."},{"by":"gate-keeper","text":"Or you blinked."}]},{"id":"B-pair-12","who":["fortune-teller","fair-baker"],"when":{"stage":[2,3]},"lines":[{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"Cut the deck for me, baker. Your hands are warm. Mine haven't been since dusk."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"Floury, mind. You'll have bread on your stars."},{"by":"fortune-teller","text":"Oh. Oh, that's a good card. That's the first good card all night."},{"by":"fair-baker","text":"Flour does that. I could have told you years ago."}]},{"id":"B-pair-13","who":["ribbon-dyer","chestnut-roaster"],"when":{"stage":[1,2]},"lines":[{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"Your coals. When they came back. What colour?"},{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"Red. Same as ever. Why?"},{"by":"ribbon-dyer","text":"Not the same. Redder."},{"by":"chestnut-roaster","text":"Redder. I'll put that in. Nobody ever gives me a new bit."}]},{"id":"B-pair-14","who":["ballad-singer","captain"],"when":{"stage":[1,2]},"lines":[{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"Captain, can I put your lamps in a song? Twelve lamps flying east. It's a gift."},{"by":"captain","text":"Leave them out."},{"by":"ballad-singer","text":"Why? It's the best thing that's happened all year."},{"by":"captain","text":"Not to them."}]}]};
